            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0728" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/11a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Howard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-14T18:00:00-04:00">June 14, 1937—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. The <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> this morning published a
                    report from its correspondent in Buenos Aires to the effect that a revolt had
                    taken place in the Paraguayan Army because of its unwillingness to agree to the
                    policy of the Paraguayan Government as regards the Chaco;<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d688-f1"/> and that the fall of President Franco was imminent.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph immediately whether there is any basis of truth in this
                    report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
